om2
note compiler/rebuild.om: after /si has fetched the projects, rebuild each layer of the stack from
note source and compare it with what is published, layer by layer from the seed upward. Pure seeded
note Omega. Table-driven: the layers, their repositories and their commands are the rows of
note layers.tsv beside repos.tsv; this program holds no layer, repository or command of its own.
note
note Build with the seeded compiler (compiler/README.md names the pins):
note   omc < compiler/rebuild.om > rebuild && chmod +x rebuild
note Run:
note   rebuild check LAYERS
note   rebuild run LAYERS REPOS DIR WORK [hw=yes] [wrap=WORDS]
note LAYERS  layers.tsv: the line "layers TAB N" (N from 2 to 999), the header line
note         "layer TAB repo TAB needs TAB command TAB artifact TAB compare", then one row per step:
note         layer    1..N, rows in layer order, every layer from 1 to N with at least one row
note         repo     a project name; its commit is the head repos.tsv gives it
note         needs    any; aarch64-linux; macos (this is a Linux program, so always NOT_RUN); or
note                  pci:VVVV:DDDD, a hardware row: it runs only with hw=yes and a PCI device
note                  VVVV:DDDD under /sys/bus/pci/devices, else NOT_RUN, never PASS
note         command  the repository's own documented command, run by /bin/sh -c in its clone,
note                  or - when it has none (NOT_RUN no documented rebuild command)
note         artifact the file the command builds, a path in the clone, or -
note         compare  a path in the clone whose bytes at the commit the artifact must equal, or -
note REPOS   repos.tsv: each project's commit is its head there
note DIR     the directory /si fetched into, one clone per project named as in repos.tsv
note WORK    an existing directory: a log per row, layer-L-R.log (R the row number), and the
note         files git writes
note check validates LAYERS and prints "rebuild: table ok: N layers, R rows". run validates it the
note same way, then takes the rows in order and prints one line per row:
note   PASS | layer L | repo | commit C | rc 0 | sha256 S | log G | cmd COMMAND
note   FAIL <why> | layer L | ...     a clone not at its commit, a command exiting nonzero, a
note                                  missing artifact, or an artifact whose sha256 differs from
note                                  the committed file's
note   NOT_RUN <why> | layer L | ...  needs not met here, no documented command, not fetched
note and last "REBUILD pass=P fail=F not_run=N rows=R layers=L". Exit 0 when no row FAILs and every
note row of layers 1 and 2 PASSes, else 1. A refused table: exit 1, one stderr line starting
note "rebuild: " and nothing run. A usage error: exit 2.
note A command runs with stdin /dev/null and stdout and stderr in its log. Exec hands a child an
note empty environment, so the command gets HOME, PATH, USER, LOGNAME, LANG, LC_ALL, TMPDIR,
note CARGO_HOME and RUSTUP_HOME copied from this program's own, where set, through /usr/bin/env.
note wrap=WORDS puts WORDS, split at spaces, between those and /bin/sh, for example a CPU pool:
note wrap=flock /path/pool.lock taskset -c 4,5.
note SHA-256 (fn kinit to fn finish) is copied unchanged from compiler/gate.om, which copied it
note from omega-mv om/sha256/sha256-om2.om at f4df82394e35893dcf1354dda69a2fe028d94bc1
note (Apache-2.0, FIPS 180-4).

text tpre "rebuild: "
text tnl "\n"
text tusage "usage: rebuild check LAYERS | rebuild run LAYERS REPOS DIR WORK [hw=yes] [wrap=WORDS]\n"
text tcheck "check"
text trun "run"
text thw "hw=yes"
text twrap "wrap="
text targ "cannot read a command-line argument"
text topen "cannot open "
text tbig "file over its buffer: "
text tnodir "WORK is not a directory: "
text tlay "layers\t"
text thdr "layer\trepo\tneeds\tcommand\tartifact\tcompare"
text mfirst "the first line must be layers TAB N, N from 2 to 999"
text mhdr "the second line must be the header layer TAB repo TAB needs TAB command TAB artifact TAB compare"
text mcols "a row needs 6 tab-separated fields: line "
text mlayer "layer is not a number from 1 to the declared count: line "
text morder "rows are not in layer order: line "
text mnorow1 "layer "
text mnorow2 " has no row"
text mrepo "bad repo name (letters, digits, . _ -, not starting with .): line "
text mneeds "needs is not any, aarch64-linux, macos or pci:VVVV:DDDD (lowercase hex): line "
text mcmd "command is empty, over 1024 bytes or has a control byte: line "
text mpath "artifact or compare is not - or a relative path without .. or control bytes: line "
text mcmp "compare needs an artifact: line "
text mmany "more than 4096 rows at line "
text tok1 "rebuild: table ok: "
text tok2 " layers, "
text tok3 " rows\n"
text nany "any"
text na64 "aarch64-linux"
text nmac "macos"
text npci "pci:"
text tdash "-"
text rmac "macOS only; this runner is a Linux program"
text ra64 "needs AArch64 Linux"
text rhw "hardware row; runs only with hw=yes, in an authorized hardware window"
text rchip "hardware row; no PCI device "
text rchip2 " here"
text rcmd "no documented rebuild command"
text rlist "not in repos.tsv, so /si does not fetch it"
text rbadh "the repos.tsv head is not 40 lowercase hex digits"
text rfetch "not fetched: no clone in DIR"
text rhead "clone is not at the repos.tsv commit; it is at "
text runk "clone HEAD cannot be read"
text rexit "command exited nonzero"
text rio "cannot write its log in WORK"
text rpkt "command, wrap and environment exceed one exec packet (4096 bytes, 64 records)"
text rart "artifact missing: "
text rcom "no committed file at the commit: "
text rdiff "artifact differs from committed "
text tsp " "
text vpass "PASS"
text vfail "FAIL "
text vnrun "NOT_RUN "
text bl " | layer "
text br " | "
text bc " | commit "
text brc " | rc "
text bsha " | sha256 "
text blog " | log "
text bcmd " | cmd "
text sum1 "REBUILD pass="
text sum2 " fail="
text sum3 " not_run="
text sum4 " rows="
text sum5 " layers="
text tself "/proc/self/exe"
text tpcid "/sys/bus/pci/devices"
text tvend "/vendor"
text tdev "/device"
text tnull "/dev/null"
text tlogp "/layer-"
text tlog ".log"
text tcom ".committed"
text tgit "/git.out"
text xenv "/usr/bin/env"
text xsh "/bin/sh"
text xc "-c"
text xgit "git"
text xrp "rev-parse"
text xhead "HEAD"
text xcf "cat-file"
text xblob "blob"
text e1 "HOME="
text e2 "PATH="
text e3 "USER="
text e4 "LOGNAME="
text e5 "LANG="
text e6 "LC_ALL="
text e7 "TMPDIR="
text e8 "CARGO_HOME="
text e9 "RUSTUP_HOME="
text hexd "0123456789abcdef"

note tb: the layers table; rp: repos.tsv
global tb uchar 1048576
global tbn ulong 1
global rp uchar 4194304
global rpn ulong 1
note rows, 12 cells each: layer, repo offset and length, needs (1 any, 2 aarch64-linux, 3 macos,
note 4 pci), command, artifact and compare offsets and lengths (4..9), line number (10), needs
note offset (11). nlay: the declared layer count; prevl: the layer of the row before
global row ulong 49152
global nrow ulong 1
global nlay ulong 1
global prevl ulong 1
note pb: the path being built; dir: DIR; wk: WORK; wr: the wrap words; cd: the clone of the row
global pb uchar 8192
global pbn ulong 1
global dir uchar 4096
global dirn ulong 1
global wk uchar 4096
global wkn ulong 1
global wr uchar 4096
global wrn ulong 1
global cd uchar 8192
global cdn ulong 1
note av: the packed argv of a child (u16 count, then u16 length and bytes per record); ovf is 1
note when a record did not fit. ev: the environment records handed on, packed the same way
global av uchar 8192
global avp ulong 1
global avc ulong 1
global ovf ulong 1
global ev uchar 4096
global evn ulong 1
global evc ulong 1
note st: a child's wait status; gb: small file reads; db: directory entries
global st uchar 4
global gb uchar 4096
global gbn ulong 1
global db uchar 32768
note the current row: its commit (cm, cmn 40 when known), exit status (crc, hrc 1 when run),
note artifact, log and committed sha256 in hex (hx, hl, hc; hsa and hlg 1 when known)
global cm uchar 40
global cmn ulong 1
global crc ulong 1
global hrc ulong 1
global hx uchar 64
global hl uchar 64
global hc uchar 64
global hsa ulong 1
global hlg ulong 1
global dg uchar 32
note tally: PASS, FAIL and NOT_RUN rows; l12: rows of layers 1 and 2 that did not PASS;
note a64: 1 when this program is an AArch64 ELF; hw: 1 with hw=yes
global tally ulong 3
global l12 ulong 1
global a64 ulong 1
global hw ulong 1

text tslash "/"
text tcolon ":"
text tempty ""

note K[0..63]: the first 32 bits of the fractional parts of the cube roots of the first 64 primes.
note Copied mechanically from seed/qualification/om2/fixtures/sha256-k.dec (tool-computed, never typed).
fn kinit k edit uint 64 to void
put k 0 0x428a2f98
put k 1 0x71374491
put k 2 0xb5c0fbcf
put k 3 0xe9b5dba5
put k 4 0x3956c25b
put k 5 0x59f111f1
put k 6 0x923f82a4
put k 7 0xab1c5ed5
put k 8 0xd807aa98
put k 9 0x12835b01
put k 10 0x243185be
put k 11 0x550c7dc3
put k 12 0x72be5d74
put k 13 0x80deb1fe
put k 14 0x9bdc06a7
put k 15 0xc19bf174
put k 16 0xe49b69c1
put k 17 0xefbe4786
put k 18 0x0fc19dc6
put k 19 0x240ca1cc
put k 20 0x2de92c6f
put k 21 0x4a7484aa
put k 22 0x5cb0a9dc
put k 23 0x76f988da
put k 24 0x983e5152
put k 25 0xa831c66d
put k 26 0xb00327c8
put k 27 0xbf597fc7
put k 28 0xc6e00bf3
put k 29 0xd5a79147
put k 30 0x06ca6351
put k 31 0x14292967
put k 32 0x27b70a85
put k 33 0x2e1b2138
put k 34 0x4d2c6dfc
put k 35 0x53380d13
put k 36 0x650a7354
put k 37 0x766a0abb
put k 38 0x81c2c92e
put k 39 0x92722c85
put k 40 0xa2bfe8a1
put k 41 0xa81a664b
put k 42 0xc24b8b70
put k 43 0xc76c51a3
put k 44 0xd192e819
put k 45 0xd6990624
put k 46 0xf40e3585
put k 47 0x106aa070
put k 48 0x19a4c116
put k 49 0x1e376c08
put k 50 0x2748774c
put k 51 0x34b0bcb5
put k 52 0x391c0cb3
put k 53 0x4ed8aa4a
put k 54 0x5b9cca4f
put k 55 0x682e6ff3
put k 56 0x748f82ee
put k 57 0x78a5636f
put k 58 0x84c87814
put k 59 0x8cc70208
put k 60 0x90befffa
put k 61 0xa4506ceb
put k 62 0xbef9a3f7
put k 63 0xc67178f2
end

note H(0): the first 32 bits of the fractional parts of the square roots of the first 8 primes
note (fixtures/sha256-iv.dec).
fn iv s edit uint 8 to void
put s 0 0x6a09e667
put s 1 0xbb67ae85
put s 2 0x3c6ef372
put s 3 0xa54ff53a
put s 4 0x510e527f
put s 5 0x9b05688c
put s 6 0x1f83d9ab
put s 7 0x5be0cd19
end

note Message schedule of the block m[o .. o+64). w is fresh: its incoming contents are never read.
note The compiler proves that every get of w reads an element written earlier in this function
note (error 27 otherwise): w[0..16) are the block's big-endian words, w[16..64) the FIPS recurrence.
fn sched w edit uint 64 fresh m view uchar * o ulong to void
q = ulong 0
x = uint 0
y = uint 0
for i ulong 16 unroll
q = add o mul i 4
x = uint get m q
x = or shl x 8 uint get m add q 1
x = or shl x 8 uint get m add q 2
put w i or shl x 8 uint get m add q 3
end
for i ulong 48 unroll
x = get w add i 1
y = get w add i 14
x = add add get w i get w add i 9 xor xor rotr x 7 rotr x 18 shr x 3
put w add i 16 add x xor xor rotr y 17 rotr y 19 shr y 10
end
end

note The 64 rounds on the chaining value s. One round body, emitted 64 times by unroll; i is a constant
note in each copy, so get kt i and get w i need no run-time check. uint arithmetic wraps mod 2^32.
note Ch(e,f,g) = (e and f) xor (not e and g) is written g xor (e and (f xor g)); Maj(a,b,c) =
note (a and b) xor (a and c) xor (b and c) is written (a and b) or (c and (a or b)). Both are bitwise
note identities. h first becomes T1, then T1 + T2, which is the next a; the names then shift by one.
note The sums are built a term per line and each Sigma in two lines through t: 12 names are live, and
note omc hands out 16 registers with no spilling (error 12 under compiler-s1/s2 for longer lines).
fn rounds s edit uint 8 w view uint 64 kt view uint 64 to void
a = get s 0
b = get s 1
c = get s 2
d = get s 3
e = get s 4
f = get s 5
g = get s 6
h = get s 7
t = uint 0
for i ulong 64 unroll
h = add h get kt i
h = add h get w i
t = xor rotr e 6 rotr e 11
t = xor t rotr e 25
h = add h t
h = add h xor g and e xor f g
d = add d h
t = xor rotr a 2 rotr a 13
t = xor t rotr a 22
h = add h t
t = and c or a b
h = add h or and a b t
t = h
h = g
g = f
f = e
e = d
d = c
c = b
b = a
a = t
end
put s 0 add get s 0 a
put s 1 add get s 1 b
put s 2 add get s 2 c
put s 3 add get s 3 d
put s 4 add get s 4 e
put s 5 add get s 5 f
put s 6 add get s 6 g
put s 7 add get s 7 h
end

note One block m[o .. o+64) into s. sched and rounds stay calls: inlined, their names would share
note one 16-register frame with this function's parameters (no spilling, error 12).
fn compress s edit uint 8 w edit uint 64 kt view uint 64 m view uchar * o ulong to void
sched w m o
rounds s w kt
end

note The whole blocks of m (len m is a multiple of 64 and at most 2^25, so under 2^19 passes).
fn run s edit uint 8 w edit uint 64 kt view uint 64 m view uchar * to void
for j ulong shr len m 6
compress s w kt m shl j 6
end
end

note The whole blocks of m (len m a multiple of 64). A rolled loop traps 4 after 1000000 passes
note (OMEGESE.md section 2; omc s_for), so m is cut into runs of 2^25 bytes (2^19 blocks):
note len m = top * 2^44 + mid * 2^25 + rest, and no loop passes 2^20 times. top reaches 1000000
note only above 1.7e19 bytes, which no AArch64 address space holds.
fn blocks s edit uint 8 w edit uint 64 kt view uint 64 m view uchar * to void
q = ulong 0
for a ulong shr len m 44
for b ulong 0x80000
run s w kt part m q 0x2000000
q = add q 0x2000000
end
end
for b ulong and shr len m 25 0x7ffff
run s w kt part m q 0x2000000
q = add q 0x2000000
end
run s w kt part m q sub len m q
end

note Pad the k pending bytes already in p (k < 64; p was all zero past them): 0x80, zeros, and the
note 64-bit big-endian bit length of the n-byte message in the last 8 bytes of one or two blocks.
fn finish s edit uint 8 w edit uint 64 kt view uint 64 p edit uchar 128 k ulong n ulong to void
put p k 0x80
e = ulong 64
if ge k 56
e = 128
end
bits = shl n 3
for i ulong 8 unroll
put p sub e add i 1 uchar and shr bits mul i 8 0xff
end
compress s w kt view p 0
if eq e 128
compress s w kt view p 64
end
end


fn say t view uchar * to void
w = write 1 t 0 len t
end
fn sayn v ulong to void
d = new uchar 24 0
x = v
k = ulong 0
while or gt x 0 eq k 0 bound 24
put d k uchar add rem x 10 48
k = add k 1
x = div x 10
end
while gt k 0 bound 24
k = sub k 1
w = write 1 d k 1
end
end
fn die t view uchar * to void
w = write 2 tpre 0 len tpre
w = write 2 t 0 len t
w = write 2 tnl 0 1
exit 1
end
fn badline t view uchar * ln ulong to void
say tpre
say t
sayn ln
say tnl
exit 1
end
fn patharg a ulong to void
n = argread a pb 0 8192
if le n 0
die targ
end
put pbn 0 ulong n
end
fn pc t view uchar * to void
put pbn 0 0
pa t
end
fn pa t view uchar * to void
p = get pbn 0
for i ulong len t
put pb add p i get t i
end
put pbn 0 add p len t
end
fn pt o ulong n ulong to void
p = get pbn 0
for i ulong n
put pb add p i get tb add o i
end
put pbn 0 add p n
end
fn pn v ulong to void
d = new uchar 24 0
x = v
k = ulong 0
while or gt x 0 eq k 0 bound 24
put d k uchar add rem x 10 48
k = add k 1
x = div x 10
end
while gt k 0 bound 24
k = sub k 1
p = get pbn 0
put pb p get d k
put pbn 0 add p 1
end
end
fn eqt o ulong n ulong t view uchar * to bool
if ne n len t
ret false
end
for i ulong n
if ne get tb add o i get t i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
fn num o ulong n ulong to ulong
v = ulong 0
if eq n 0
ret 0
end
for i ulong n
c = get tb add o i
if or lt c 48 gt c 57
ret 0
end
v = add mul v 10 ulong sub c 48
if gt v 999
ret 0
end
end
ret v
end
fn nam o ulong n ulong to bool
if eq n 0
ret false
end
if eq get tb o 46
ret false
end
for i ulong n
c = get tb add o i
ok = and ge c 65 le c 90
ok = or ok and ge c 97 le c 122
ok = or ok and ge c 48 le c 57
ok = or ok or eq c 46 or eq c 45 eq c 95
if not ok
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
fn rel o ulong n ulong to bool
if eq n 0
ret false
end
if eq get tb o 47
ret false
end
for i ulong n
c = get tb add o i
if or lt c 33 gt c 126
ret false
end
if eq c 46
if lt add i 1 n
if eq get tb add add o i 1 46
ret false
end
end
end
end
ret true
end
fn hexchar c uchar to bool
ret or and ge c 48 le c 57 and ge c 97 le c 102
end
fn needs o ulong n ulong to ulong
if eqt o n nany
ret 1
end
if eqt o n na64
ret 2
end
if eqt o n nmac
ret 3
end
if ne n 13
ret 0
end
if not eqt o 4 npci
ret 0
end
if ne get tb add o 8 58
ret 0
end
for i ulong 9
if ne i 4
if not hexchar get tb add add o 4 i
ret 0
end
end
end
ret 4
end
fn parserow s ulong e ulong ln ulong to void
fs = new ulong 6 0
fnn = new ulong 6 0
if true
f = ulong 0
q = s
x = s
while le q e bound 1048577
endf = eq q e
if not endf
endf = eq get tb q 9
end
if endf
if ge f 6
badline mcols ln
end
put fs f x
put fnn f sub q x
f = add f 1
x = add q 1
end
q = add q 1
end
if ne f 6
badline mcols ln
end
end
v = num get fs 0 get fnn 0
if or eq v 0 gt v get nlay 0
badline mlayer ln
end
if lt v get prevl 0
badline morder ln
end
put prevl 0 v
if not nam get fs 1 get fnn 1
badline mrepo ln
end
k = needs get fs 2 get fnn 2
if eq k 0
badline mneeds ln
end
if true
cn = get fnn 3
if or eq cn 0 gt cn 1024
badline mcmd ln
end
for j ulong cn
c = get tb add get fs 3 j
if or lt c 32 gt c 126
badline mcmd ln
end
end
if not rel get fs 4 get fnn 4
badline mpath ln
end
if not rel get fs 5 get fnn 5
badline mpath ln
end
if eqt get fs 4 get fnn 4 tdash
if not eqt get fs 5 get fnn 5 tdash
badline mcmp ln
end
end
end
r = get nrow 0
if ge r 4096
badline mmany ln
end
b = mul r 12
put row b v
put row add b 1 get fs 1
put row add b 2 get fnn 1
put row add b 3 k
put row add b 4 get fs 3
put row add b 5 get fnn 3
put row add b 6 get fs 4
put row add b 7 get fnn 4
put row add b 8 get fs 5
put row add b 9 get fnn 5
put row add b 10 ln
put row add b 11 get fs 2
put nrow 0 add r 1
end
fn coverage to void
for i ulong get nlay 0
found = false
for j ulong get nrow 0
ly = get row mul j 12
if eq ly add i 1
found = true
end
end
if not found
say tpre
say mnorow1
sayn add i 1
say mnorow2
say tnl
exit 1
end
end
end
fn parse to void
n = get tbn 0
p = ulong 0
ln = ulong 0
while lt p n bound 1048577
s = p
while lt p n bound 1048577
if eq get tb p 10
break
end
p = add p 1
end
e = p
p = add p 1
ln = add ln 1
if eq ln 1
if lt sub e s 8
die mfirst
end
if not eqt s 7 tlay
die mfirst
end
v = num add s 7 sub sub e s 7
if lt v 2
die mfirst
end
put nlay 0 v
else
if eq ln 2
if not eqt s sub e s thdr
die mhdr
end
else
parserow s e ln
end
end
end
if lt ln 2
die mhdr
end
coverage
end
fn loadtab to void
fd = fopen pb 0 get pbn 0 524288 0
if lt fd 0
die topen
end
p = ulong 0
while lt p 1048576 bound 1048577
k = read int fd tb p sub 1048576 p
if lt k 0
die topen
end
if eq k 0
break
end
p = add p ulong k
end
c = fclose int fd
if ge p 1048576
die tbig
end
put tbn 0 p
parse
end
fn loadrepos to void
fd = fopen pb 0 get pbn 0 524288 0
if lt fd 0
die topen
end
p = ulong 0
while lt p 4194304 bound 4194305
k = read int fd rp p sub 4194304 p
if lt k 0
die topen
end
if eq k 0
break
end
p = add p ulong k
end
c = fclose int fd
if ge p 4194304
die tbig
end
put rpn 0 p
end
note locate the row's name and copy its manifest commit; false if absent or malformed.
fn commit b ulong to bool
put cmn 0 0
p = ulong 0
while lt p get rpn 0 bound 4194305
s = p
while lt p get rpn 0 bound 4194305
if or eq get rp p 9 eq get rp p 10
break
end
p = add p 1
end
same = eq sub p s get row add b 2
if same
for i ulong sub p s
co = add get row add b 1 i
cv = get tb co
if ne get rp add s i cv
same = false
end
end
end
if same
p = add p 1
while lt p get rpn 0 bound 4194305
if eq get rp p 9
break
end
p = add p 1
end
p = add p 1
s = p
while lt p get rpn 0 bound 4194305
if or eq get rp p 9 eq get rp p 10
break
end
p = add p 1
end
if ne sub p s 40
ret false
end
for i ulong 40
v = get rp add s i
if not hexchar v
ret false
end
put cm i v
end
put cmn 0 40
ret true
end
while lt p get rpn 0 bound 4194305
if eq get rp p 10
break
end
p = add p 1
end
p = add p 1
end
ret false
end
fn aa t view uchar * to void
n = len t
p = get avp 0
if or gt add add p 2 n 4096 ge get avc 0 64
put ovf 0 1
ret
end
put av p uchar and n 255
put av add p 1 uchar shr n 8
for i ulong n
put av add add p 2 i get t i
end
put avp 0 add add p 2 n
put avc 0 add get avc 0 1
end
fn ap to void
